RES osdtriplet
! ---- Constraint commands work inside AUT loop ----
! Run a short optimisation: CCY S3 + THC S3 as variables, TAS as constraint.
! LCON lists constraints after the loop; DCON ALL clears them.
AUT
CCY S3 0
THC S3 0
TAS = 0.01
TCO = 0.005
GO
LCON
DCON ALL
LCON
! ---- IMP sets improvement goal (silent state setter) ----
IMP 0.001
! ---- AUTOFUNC reports current autofunc (none defined) ----
AUTOFUNC
! ---- COST and WEIGHT: need CAPFN context ----
FOB 0
CAPFN
COST 1 6
WEIGHT 1 6
! ---- PRICE ALL: no data in this lens ----
PRICE ALL
! ---- DEFORM: no deformable surfaces in osdtriplet ----
DEFORM
! ---- XXF P: Newtonian equation, find missing value (two given) ----
XXF P -50 25
! ---- XXFF P: Newtonian equation with 4 terms (find one) ----
XXFF P -50 25 30
! ---- OIF P: object-image-focal calculation ----
OIF P -200 50
! ---- DO: repeat FIR 3 times (deterministic) ----
DO FIR 1 3

! ---- AUT with no variables: must not crash ----
! Regression: AUT;GO without any variable used to ERROR STOP inside the slsqp
! initialization (killing the whole program).  Now it prints a clear message
! and returns.  Both the bare form and the with-constraint form are covered.
RES osdtriplet
AUT
GO
AUT
EFL = 50
GO
DCON ALL

! ---- Unified merit entries: operand vs constraint roles ----
! NAME target [weight] (no operator) adds an OBJECTIVE term, minimized as
! weight*(value-target)**2; NAME = value adds a hard constraint.  LCON lists
! both with their role.  The merit block round-trips through SAV/RES
! (including the weight), and DCON ALL clears operands too (historically
! operands survived and leaked across lens loads).
RES osdtriplet
TAR
SPO 0.0 2.0
EFL 55 0.5
TAS = 0.01
GO
LCON
SAV merittest
RES merittest
LCON
DCON ALL
LCON

! ---- General constraints: set/query + SAV/RES round-trip + reset on load ----
! MXT/MNT/MNE/MNA/MAE apply to variable thicknesses at AUT;GO.  Modified
! values persist in the saved merit block and reset to defaults on lens load.
RES osdtriplet
AUT
MXT 14.0
MNE 1.5
MXT
GO
LCON
SAV gencontest
RES gencontest
LCON
RES osdtriplet
LCON

! ---- GENCON: master switch for the general constraints ----
! GENCON NO turns all five off (LCON says so, and it round-trips through
! SAV/RES); bare GENCON queries; UPD CON; GENCON YES; GO turns them back on
! without optimizing (the AUTUI path).  GENCON outside a loop is an error.
GENCON NO
RES osdtriplet
AUT
GENCON NO
GENCON
GO
LCON
SAV genconoff
RES genconoff
LCON
UPD CON
GENCON YES
GENCON
GO
LCON
RES osdtriplet
LCON

! ---- General constraints active in an optimization ----
! THC S1 makes the first element's thickness a variable: bounds [MNT, MXT]
! apply and an MNE edge constraint is generated (report shows the MNE row).
! With MNE 2.5 (start edge 2.30) the optimizer must thicken the element;
! ETH shows the edge moved toward the limit (exact attainment is bounded by
! the solver's loose iteration caps -- max_iter/toldf tuning, not the
! constraint wiring).
RES osdtriplet
THC S1 0
AUT
MNE 2.5
GO
ETH
SUR SA

! ---- Full optimization: singlet with a fixed EFL (the originally-broken case) ----
! Regression for the frozen-typed-store bug: variable values applied during
! optimization never reached the paraxial/real traces (the typed store was
! not refreshed), every merit evaluation saw the ORIGINAL lens, gradients
! were zero, and slsqp aborted immediately with "positive directional
! derivative".  Now: spot is minimized subject to EFL = 50, converging
! within acc (optim%imp), and the returned solution is applied to the lens.
RES OsdSinglet
CCY S1 0
AUT
EFL = 50
GO
FIR

! ---- UPD CON edit of an SPO operand (the AUTUI edit path) ----
! Regression: "SPO <targ> <weight>" inside the UPD CON loop fell through to
! the spot-PLOT branch (never updating), and GO leaked CON_UPDATE_LOOP.  Now
! the entry at CHA n is updated in place and the loop closes.
RES OsdSinglet
TAR
SPO 0.0 1.0
EFL = 50
GO
LCON
UPD CON
CHA 1
SPO 0.0 1000
GO
LCON
DCON ALL

! ---- Paraxial ray operands: UMX..ICY with [Sk] [Wm] [Zn] qualifiers ----
! U = exit angle, H = height, I = incidence angle (index*i); M = marginal,
! C = chief; X/Y = plane.  Defaults: image surface, reference wavelength,
! active zoom position.  Qualifiers show in LCON and round-trip through
! SAV/RES; bad qualifiers are rejected (non-paraxial names take none, Zn must
! be the active position).
RES osdtriplet
AUT
UMY = -0.1
HMY S3 W2 = 3.9
IMY S2 > -0.3
HCX SI 0 2
ICY Z1 = 0.2
UMY Z2 = 0
EFL S3 = 50
UMY W9 = 0
UMY S99 = 0
GO
LCON
SAV paraxtest
RES paraxtest
LCON
UPD CON
CHA 2
HMY S4 W3 = 3.8
GO
LCON
DCON ALL

! A paraxial constraint drives an optimization: the singlet's marginal ray
! exit angle at the image (UMY, i.e. the F-number) is constrained with the
! back curvature as the variable; the report lists UMY with its value.
RES OsdSinglet
CCY S2 0
AUT
UMY = -0.08
GO
FIR
DCON ALL
